# i18n-bilingual — empty env templates (mirrors the `env:` list in module.manifest).
# The generator appends these (blank) to the project's .env.example section.
#
# OPTIONAL. This module works with zero configuration: it ships Arabic + English,
# and the active default locale comes from the base's NEXT_PUBLIC_DEFAULT_LOCALE
# (set by --locale / the preset). SUPPORTED_LOCALES just RECORDS which locales the
# project supports. To actually add or remove a locale you edit i18n/config.js and
# add its dictionary (locales/<code>.json) — see the module README.
# Never commit real values.
SUPPORTED_LOCALES=
